<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania 91-day T-bill gains further.</title>
<headline>Lithuania 91-day T-bill gains further.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on 91-day Lithuanian Treasury bills climbed to 10.50 percent at auction on Monday after registering 10.16 percent last week, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID   SOLD</p>
<p>  91-day     10.50	10.16     9.25/11/25  50   85.272  50</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction is February 27 and the paper matures on May 29.</p>
<p>The next auction is on Tuesday when 40 million litas of 91-day paper will be offered for sale. -- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 52</p>
</text>
